{
  "question_text": "Write a Python function that calculates the **Accuracy Score** of a model's predictions. Accuracy measures the ratio of correct predictions to the total number of predictions.\r\n\r\nThe Accuracy formula is:\r\n\r\nAccuracy = Number of correct predictions / Total number of predictions\r\n\r\n**Parameters**\r\n\r\n- `y_true` (list[int]): True labels\r\n- `y_pred` (list[int]): Predicted labels\r\n\r\n**Returns**\r\n\r\n- float: The accuracy score, rounded to four decimal places\r\n\r\n**Requirements**\r\n\r\n- Compare each true label with the corresponding predicted label\r\n- Count the number of matches\r\n- Divide by the total number of predictions\r\n- Do not use sklearn's accuracy_score function",
  "short_text": "Calculate Accuracy Score",
